      "value": "@{5ba7e0881a53843243b76790|full_name}: yea but not the same shit, colliders in VRC are like insanely taxing with its ludicrously idiotic single-core process limitation. Imagine having a constant scan on somebody's model every tick of its refresh rate (default of 90 updates per second) that tells it to check the placement of the colliders and if any of them are interacting with the dynamic bones. Every single bone that a collider is registered to interact with calls for another check. Imagine that shit when some gayass furry model or dumbass weeb model with 120 dynamic bones all with hand colliders registered for their lusty model loads into your instance. That's 120 x 2 = 240 checks every tick. And that's for 2 fricking hands. To make shit worse the single-core limitation is like trying to fill water in a bottle with a showerhead.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
