      "value": "@{5b78615a5f267b35afbdcea4|full_name}: Yes. Which is why there is a dynamic bone limiter. Like they said, this is already a feature. Clearly you haven't used it properly. Changing the appropriate values in the config.json sucks, but it does work. There are two limits: max transforms (total dynamic bones) and collision check count. If the max transforms is surpassed all dynamic bones on the model are disabled. If the collision checks are surpassed all collisions are disabled on the avatar but the dynamic bones keep working unless it also surpasses the maximum transforms. What VRC need to do is better communicate this and add proper UI to change this in the menu ingame.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
