      "value": "@{5c8ff1b1f7d44e7de9d0203d|full_name}: VRC's avatar rating is so fucked up already that if i have a model with 32 material slots but use the exact same single material on everything it will count as 32 materials which in no way should count as a \"poor performing avatar\", unless VRC is retarded and doesnt utilize Unity batching.\nI can put a single \"unimportant\" mixed light with the range of .1 meter and it would call my avatar \"very poor\".\nBut I could put 100 CPU intensive dynamic bone collision checks and it would be labeled as \"average\".\nSo yes, we do need some more control on what we want to see for the sake of performance reasons.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
