      "value": "@{5c8ff1b1f7d44e7de9d0203d|full_name}: Correct me if I'm wrong but these two systems don't interact. The performance limiter takes the avatar performance rating and disables it entirely base upon maximum performance rating (grey-man). The Dynamic bone limiter independently disables the dynamic bone components or the collisions if they are surpassed (graceful downgrade).\nThis means that if an avatar that otherwise meets a 'medium' rating with the exception of the dynamic bones stats (but with them it is 'poor') it can still be disabled by the performance limiter even if your dynamic bone limiter would have disabled them. This basically means an avatar that would otherwise be graceful downgraded by the bone limiter can be grey-manned instead by the performance limiter.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
