      "value": "@{5c172a680f1f05085fcfd546|full_name}: i believe your explanations is right and make sense.\nhowever they do interact together in the form of layers\nfrom my observations, it works like this\nAvatar stats > Trust System (hard block, won't downgrade) > Performance Ranking Limiter (graceful downgrade when possible) > Dynamic Bones Limiter (disables dyn.bones component past the treshold)\nthe way i configure my personnal settings, is:\n1- Set the Trust System to your liking (personally i set it to custom, but is very similar to Maximum)\n2- Set performance limiter to \"LOW\"\n3- Set the trigger for the dyn.bones to limit at the treshold of very low rank for bones (256transform and 256collision)\nthat makes it sure that if an avatar is low, medium or good, they will never get there dyn.bones blocked, won't be grey-man or limited-man, and won't show feature i don't want them to\nif they are very low ONLY because of dynamic bones, they will get the same treatment as if it was gradefully downgraded by the performance limiter (meaning they should still be visible)\ni can afford those transform because i have a decent rig, your mileage may vary however.\nthis gives me the most flexibility to adjust settings, and make sure i don't have avatars blocked where they shouldn't be.\ni also avoid activating people manually because this activates ALL their features (effectively override any safety systems)\nsince i don't care for custom animations, light sources and particles, this works for me.\nif someone wants to show me their content, at least i won't get forced into it\nhope this helps\nhttps://docs.vrchat.com/docs/avatar-performance-ranking-system#section-minimum-displayed-performance-rank-on-pc\nhttps://docs.vrchat.com/docs/avatar-dynamic-bone-limits#section-modifying-the-dynamic-bone-limits\n@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name} maybe you could confirm if my theory about those limiting system are right ?\ni would love to write a proper tutorial for this, but i don't want to spread the wrong idea",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
