      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "i also have made a post in another thread how i would like to have more granular control over avatars limiting function. either by global modifiers, choosing my own limits where the limiters should kick in (in an example, let's say i have an avatar with 120k poly, but 1 mesh and 1 material. this would technically be a good+ ranking avatar. but it'll get blocked.\nit would make it a bit more complex, but much more versatile in my opinion. the same way we have custom limtier for particles trails and dynamic bones\nor another way of implementing it, would be to select features activation via the menu, based on blueprint ID (or particular user, or both...)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
